{"Title":"An Act designating a certain bridge in the town of Dedham as the Honorable Kelly A. Timilty memorial bridge","BillNumber":"H3383","DocketNumber":"HD3739","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T14:21:18.157"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T14:21:18.1566667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3383/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative McMurtry of Dedham, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3383) of Paul McMurtry that the bridge on Ames Street over the Charles River in the town of Dedham be designated as the Honorable Kelly A. Timilty memorial bridge.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tBridge D-05-005 on Ames Street, over the Charles River in the Town of Dedham, shall be designated and known as the “Honorable Kelly A. Timilty Memorial Bridge” in recognition of Kelly A. Timilty. Kelly was a beloved public servant who served nine consecutive terms before five governors on the Governor's Council. Kelly was the youngest child of Joseph F. Timilty, former state senator, and the sister of the Honorable James E. Timilty. She passed away before her time on January 31, 2012. The Massachusetts Department of Transportation shall erect and maintain a suitable marker bearing the designation in compliance with the standards of the department.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"S29","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[{"AmendmentNumber":"1","ParentBillNumber":"H3383","Branch":"House","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3383/Branches/House/Amendments/1/"}]}